This plugin talks to Herdr (https://github.com/herdrdev/herdr, Apache-2.0)
over its socket API and bundles one file from that project for its tests:
tests/fixtures/herdr-api-0.8.2.schema.json, the published JSON schema of the
Herdr 0.8.2 socket API.

It also bundles these third-party assets unmodified, each with its licence
next to it:

- assets/icons/lucide/: the Lucide icon set (https://github.com/lucide-icons/lucide),
  as packaged by @iconify-json/lucide,
  Copyright (c) 2026 Lucide Icons and Contributors, ISC License; the icons
  Lucide derives from Feather are Copyright (c) 2013-present Cole Bemis, MIT
  License. Both texts are in assets/icons/lucide/LICENSE.
- assets/fonts/inter/: Inter 4.1 (https://github.com/rsms/inter), SIL Open
  Font License 1.1, in assets/fonts/inter/OFL.txt.
- assets/fonts/geist-mono/: Geist Mono 1.7.2 (https://github.com/vercel/geist-font),
  SIL Open Font License 1.1, in assets/fonts/geist-mono/OFL.txt.

The whiteboard page (web/dist/, built from web/) also bundles npm packages,
minified and tree-shaken: React, the canvas v2 renderer's charting and 3D
libraries, Mermaid, Vega, d3 and p5 for live visuals, and Excalidraw with its
dependencies for the classic canvas (v1). web/dist/MANIFEST.json lists every
bundled package with its version, and the build copies each one's licence and
notice texts into web/dist/licenses/. Of the Apache-2.0 packages among them,
only echarts ships a NOTICE file, quoted below; browser-fs-access and crc-32
(Apache-2.0) and dompurify (MPL-2.0 or Apache-2.0) ship none, and their
licences are in web/dist/licenses/. The packages that call for a note here:

- echarts 6.1.0 (https://echarts.apache.org), Apache License 2.0; its NOTICE:
  "Apache ECharts, Copyright 2017-2026 The Apache Software Foundation. This
  product includes software developed at The Apache Software Foundation
  (https://www.apache.org/)."
- zrender 6.1.0 (a dependency of echarts), BSD 3-Clause License.
- tslib 2.3.0 (a dependency of echarts), 0BSD; tslib 2.8.1 is bundled for
  other packages under the same licence.
- echarts-gl 2.1.0 (https://github.com/ecomfe/echarts-gl), BSD 3-Clause
  License per its LICENSE file (its package.json says MIT; the LICENSE text is
  what ships).
- claygl 1.3.0 (a dependency of echarts-gl), BSD 2-Clause License; the build
  replaces one `new Function` in claygl/src/compositor/createCompositor.js with
  an arithmetic evaluator so the page's Content-Security-Policy holds.
- three 0.186.1 (https://threejs.org), MIT License.
- d3-scale-chromatic 3.1.0 (https://d3js.org/d3-scale-chromatic/), ISC License,
  Copyright 2010-2024 Mike Bostock. It is not an Apache-2.0 package, but it
  embeds ColorBrewer's colour schemes, Copyright 2002 Cynthia Brewer, Mark
  Harrower and The Pennsylvania State University, under an "Apache-Style
  Software License ... Apache License, Version 2.0"; both texts ship in
  web/dist/licenses/d3-scale-chromatic.txt, so a reader auditing the
  Apache-2.0 list above finds this one here.
